 The plan must already be in its final state, including its own merge-gate checkbox (final verification wave F2) marked `[x]`, at the moment reviewers are dispatched and this digest is taken - no plan edit may follow. `plan_sha256` binds whatever bytes existed at hash time, so hashing before that mark would seal an unfrozen plan and let the gate's own required output invalidate its own binding.
 
-**OpenSpec change folders.** A `--plan` that is a directory holding `gate.md` is a folder plan: Phase 0.6 runs `--plan-only --plan <change-dir>`, and the folder obeys the file-plan rules (Risk tier, Mandatory class, the one-auditor rule, the fix-round cap) with `gate.md` as the `## Merge gate` section. `validate-gate-record.mjs` and `GC` read the folder once, through a snapshot that opens each file `O_NOFOLLOW` and refuses symlinks, FIFOs and any file above 1 MiB. That one snapshot feeds the OpenSpec checks (`validate-openspec-change.mjs`'s rules), the criteria and the bundle: a manifest of `<sha256>  <path>` lines sorted by path, then each file under a `===== <path> =====` line. `plan_sha256` is the sha256 of the bundle, so it is not `shasum` of any one file; take it from the `GC snapshot` output, whose `PLAN <path>` copy is the bundle and is the plan the reviewers read. Any added, deleted or edited file in the folder fails `plan_sha256`. The review criteria are the `### Requirement:` blocks of the specs with their Negative control scenarios; a change with none (`skip_specs: true`, rename-only deltas) carries a `- Feature-specific criteria:` block in `gate.md` instead. The record's `mandatory_class` and `whole_diff` must equal `gate.md`.
